<p>The brand is the <strong>square</strong>: a capital S and a dot at its cap line, centred on a tile <em>as one group</em>. The dot is a <strong>recording light</strong> — the site is on air, somebody is publishing — and it is the accent, so the one coloured thing in the header is the same colour as the one coloured thing everywhere else. The <strong>wordmark</strong> is the same pair with the rest of the name between them: the dot lands on the last letter whatever that letter is.</p>

<h2>The square</h2>
<p>The first letter on a tile, with the dot at its top right, and the pair centred on the tile as a group — not the letter alone, which is what the favicon, the profile art and every export now agree on. The radius is a <strong>share of the tile</strong> (26%), so the shape holds at 16px and at 800px; a fixed radius makes a small mark look square and a large one look like a pill.</p>
