<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-logo-type-in</code></td><td>The letters arrive one after another, up through the baseline; the dot pops in after the last. Needs <code>data-im-split="chars"</code> on the type (the partial adds it) and <code>im-motion.js</code>.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-logo-drop</code></td><td>The dot falls onto the cap line, bounces once, settles. The letters are already there: the light switching on is the whole event.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-logo-reveal</code></td><td>The word rises through a slot cut on its own baseline; the dot blinks on at the end.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-logo-morph</code></td><td>Wordmark → square → wordmark, forever: the letters after the S fold away while a tile grows behind the pair, then it all comes back. One element that knows how to be both lockups, so an intro can open on the name and close on the mark.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-logo-states</code></td><td>The dot cycles through what a recorder has: record (the dot), play (a triangle), stop (a square), record. A clip-path morph, in the accent throughout.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
