<h2 id="cut-out">Cut out</h2>
<p>Two ways for the letters to be a window instead of ink. <code>im-logo-cutout</code> fills the letters with whatever <code>--im-logo-cut</code> holds — a gradient, a pattern, a photograph — and drifts it slowly so the window is felt to be one; <code>--im-logo-cut-opacity</code> says how strong it is and <code>--im-logo-cut-blend</code> how it meets what is under it. The dot stays solid: a light does not have a picture in it. <code>im-logo-knockout</code> is the other way round: the tile is solid and the letters are <em>holes</em> in it — a white tile with black letters, screened over the ground, so the black becomes a window. It needs something behind it; <code>im-logo-stage</code> is that something, with the picture or pattern as its ground.</p>
